t if needed\n","exq.qs1.4.ok":true,"exq.qs1.3":"1.\tIdentity need: State purpose and business reason for data.\n2.\tAuthorization: Complete access request form and get sign-off from Information/ Data Owner\n3.\tProvision: IT Security grants role-based access for a limited time.\n4.\tAudit: All access to sensitive data is logged and reviewed monthly by Compliance\n5.\tReturn: Access revoked once purpose is complete.\n","exq.qs1.3.ok":true,"exq.qs1.5":"1.\tVerify Sources: Only use data from approved systems.\n2.\tUse a Template: Follow Investecâs standard report template and check required sections.\n3.\tAccuracy Check: Cross-check numbers and do peer review before sending.\n4.\tRelevance Filter: Only include information that answers the purpose.\n5.\tCompliance Check: Ensure it meets policy, SLA definitions, and data protection rules like POPIA.\n6.\tFinal Sign-off: lGet manager approval before distribution.\n\n","exq.qs1.5.ok":true,"selfassess-0":true,"selfassess-1":true,"selfassess-2":true,"selfassess-3":true,"selfassess-4":true,"selfassess.savedAt":"2026-09-15T13:14:10.493Z"},"exercises":{"qs1":{"best":46,"last":46,"total":62,"attempts":3}},"quizzes":{}},"10135":{"activities":{"Lesson & Training Aids":false,"Summative Assessment":true,"Formative Assessment":true},"quizzes":{"q-alignment":{"best":4,"total":4,"attempts":3,"history":[{"score":4,"total":4,"date":"2026-08-13T06:07:12.662Z"},{"score":1,"total":4,"date":"2026-08-13T06:05:14.322Z"},{"score":3,"total":4,"date":"2026-07-24T08:23:14.809Z"}]},"q-so13":{"best":10,"total":10,"attempts":1,"history":[{"score":10,"total":10,"date":"2026-08-13T06:09:37.976Z"}]},"q-friday1":{"best":10,"total":10,"attempts":1,"history":[{"score":10,"total":10,"date":"2026-08-13T06:24:33.815Z"}]},"q-friday2":{"best":9,"total":10,"attempts":1,"history":[{"score":9,"total":10,"date":"2026-08-13T06:30:16.611Z"}]}},"logbook":{"exq.ex1.0":"1.Communicate- If you have a problem with a person in your group, try to address it with them.\n2.Don't blame others- Avoid pointing fingers at other people.\n3. Get involved - Share ideas, suggestions, solutions and proposals with your team members.","exq.ex1.0.ok":true,"exq.ex1.1":"Asking and answering questions\nConstructive feedback\nCourtesy and respect\nPatience\nBody language, humour and friendly chat\nActive listening","exq.ex1.1.ok":true,"exq.ex1.2":"Different opinions benefit the team\nStrong feelings and emotions\nTeam roles (leader and others)\nConflict happens and can be managed","exq.ex1.2.ok":true,"exq.ex1.3":"Actively help the team\nKnow the team's goals and objectives\nResources and clearing obstacles\nMilestones and tracking progress\nSuggest procedures and share","exq.ex1.3.ok":true,"exq.ex1.4":"Involve others and keep them informed\nListen respectfully\nShare information\nSeek every memberâs input\nInclude everyone, one at a time","exq.ex1.4.ok":true,"exq.ex1.5":"The leader's position\nActions agreed by the team\nDefined roles\nResponsibility for managing the project","exq.ex1.5.ok":true,"exq.ex1.6":"Team agreement on actions\nNegotiation and compromise\nAgreed and satisfying roles\nWhole-team input and rotating roles","exq.ex1.6.ok":true,"exq.ex1.7":"A continual balancing act\nIndividual and personal needs\nTeam needs\nAgendas on the table\nAcknowledging needs as a team","exq.ex1.7.ok":true,"exq.ex2.0":"Uncover hidden agendas\nKnow personal needs and hopes\nAsk for and seek input\nAcknowledge needs openly","exq.ex2.0.ok":true,"exq.ex2.1":"Clear team mission or purpose\nGround rules\nDefined responsibilities\nModel commitment and enthusiasm\nDepersonalize conflict","exq.ex2.1.ok":true,"exq.ex2.2":"Meetings and deadlines kept\nCome prepared\nEnergy and enthusiasm\nDelivering what was promised, on time and courteously, and speaking well of teammates in public The shared willingness to help, back each other up and move the team's work forward","exq.ex2.2.ok":false,"exq.ex2.3":"Don't Blame Others â people in your group lose respect for you if you're constantly blaming others for not meeting deadlines.\nNo Bragging â have faith that people will recognize when good work is being done and that they'll let you know how well you're doing.\nSupport group members' ideas and take the time to help your fellow team mates, no matter the request â if you've helped them in past, they'll be more than happy to lend a helping hand.\nUncover hidden agendas and expose them to the light of day â good teams recognise that this is how trust is built","exq.ex2.3.ok":true,"exq.ex2.4":"Don't express an opinion as a fact, and explain your reasons â this will allow others to evaluate your comments more effectively.\nRestate the original idea to be sure you have correctly understood it, and compliment another's idea â some part of it may be valid and could be usable in another form.\nRespond, don't react; don't interrupt; critique the idea, not the person; be courteous; avoid jargon.","exq.ex2.4.ok":true,"exq.ex2.5":"Different opinions exist\nLet each person state their view\nAcknowledge the difference\nSeek to understand all angles","exq.ex2.5.ok":true,"exq.ex2.6":"Respectful treatment\nRespectful listening \nCourtesy\nMorale and working together","exq.ex2.6.ok":true,"exq.ex2.7":"Active listening\nCourteous answers\nSeek quiet members' input\nRecognise differences and talents\nCritique ideas, not people","exq.ex2.7.ok":true,"exq.ex2.8":"Focus on the specific behaviour\nThe behaviour, not the person\nLet them express their feeling\nTalk about it directly and promptly","exq.ex2.8.ok":true,"project.upload":"{\"name\":\"Anele Khanyile Report 10135.pdf\",\"type\":\"application/pdf\",\"size\":127217,\"uploadedAt\":\"2026-08-18T08:54:38.939Z\",\"path\":\"6ac4a7ae-93ff-46cf-bba0-e3eb925c2c59/logbook/msyffexn-Anele_Khanyile_Report_10135.pdf\"}","exq.ex4.0":"Cape Town Tourism works with government, businesses and communities to improve visitor safety and security.\nThe Provincial Government and the City of Cape Town support the Safety and Security Plan.\nSouth African Police Service, emergency services and law enforcement agencies help respond to incidents quickly.\nCommunity representatives, citizens and tourism stakeholders work together to identify and address safety concerns.\nMedia partners assist by sharing accurate information and promoting public safety awareness campaigns.\nThe Tourism Victim Support Programme provides assistance and support to tourists affected by incidents.","exq.ex4.0.ok":true,"exq.ex4.0.tries":"1","exq.ex4.1":"Strong relationships help stakeholders communicate effectively and share important safety information quickly.\nGood partnerships enable faster responses to emergencies and visitor-related incidents.\nWorking together helps different organisations achieve common safety and security goals.\nSolid relationships build trust among stakeholders, communities, residents, and visitors.\nCooperation between stakeholders improves tourism experiences and supports economic growth.","exq.ex4.1.ok":true,"exq.ex4.1.tries":"1","exq.ex4.2":"Stakeholders need a safe and secure environment for residents and tourists.\nStakeholders need effective communication channels to coordinate safety and security activities.\nStakeholders need rapid emergency response systems to handle incidents efficiently.\nStakeholders need accurate and factual information to support safety awareness campaigns.\nStakeholders need cooperation and participation from communities, businesses, and government departments.\nStakeholders need victim support services to assist tourists affected by crime or emergencies.","exq.ex4.2.ok":true,"exq.ex4.2.tries":"1","exq.ex4.3":"Stakeholders use regular communication to coordinate safety and security activities effectively.\nAwareness and communication campaigns are used to educate residents and visitors.\nCommunication through local, provincial and national safety forums supports cooperation.\nEmergency response communication enables quick reporting and handling of incidents.\nMedia communication provides accurate and factual safety information to the public.","exq.ex4.3.ok":true,"exq.ex4.3.tries":"1","exq.ex4.4":"Stakeholders can hold regular meetings to discuss safety concerns openly and honestly.\nEffective communication channels allow all parties to share information and suggestions.\nParticipation in local, provincial and national safety forums encourages open discussions.\nStrong partnerships help stakeholders address problems together without misunderstandings or conflicts.\nAwareness campaigns create opportunities for stakeholders to exchange ideas and feedback.\nCo-ordination between organisations promotes transparency, trust and honest decision-making processes.","exq.ex4.4.ok":true,"exq.ex4.4.tries":"1","exq.ex4.5":"Honouring commitments helps build trust and confidence between all stakeholders.\nMeeting commitments ensures the Safety and Security Plan is implemented successfully.\nKeeping promises strengthens partnerships between government, communities and tourism stakeholders.\nHonoured commitments improve coordination and communication between all participating parties.\nFulfilling commitments helps create a safer environment for residents and visitors.","exq.ex4.5.ok":true,"exq.ex4.5.tries":"2","exq.ex1.0.marks":"4","exq.ex1.1.marks":"10","exq.ex1.2.marks":"8","exq.ex1.3.marks":"10","exq.ex1.4.marks":"2","exq.ex1.5.marks":"6","exq.ex1.6.marks":"8","exq.ex1.7.marks":"8","exq.ex2.0.marks":"8","exq.ex2.1.marks":"8","exq.ex2.3.marks":"6","exq.ex2.4.marks":"4","exq.ex2.5.marks":"8","exq.ex2.7.marks":"8","exq.ex2.8.marks":"2","exq.ex1.0.reviewedText":"1.Communicate- If you have a problem with a person in your group, try to address it with them.\n2.Don't blame others- Avoid pointing fingers at other people.\n3. Get involved - Share ideas, suggestions, solutions and proposals with your team members.","exq.ex1.1.reviewedText":"Asking and answering questions\nConstructive feedback\nCourtesy and respect\nPatience\nBod