valuate your comments more effectively.\nRestate the original idea to be sure you have correctly understood it, and compliment another's idea â some part of it may be valid and could be usable in another form.\nRespond, don't react; don't interrupt; critique the idea, not the person; be courteous; avoid jargon.","exq.ex2.5.reviewedText":"Different opinions exist\nLet each person state their view\nAcknowledge the difference\nSeek to understand all angles","exq.ex2.7.reviewedText":"Active listening\nCourteous answers\nSeek quiet members' input\nRecognise differences and talents\nCritique ideas, not people","exq.ex2.8.reviewedText":"Focus on the specific behaviour\nThe behaviour, not the person\nLet them express their feeling\nTalk about it directly and promptly"},"exercises":{"ex1":{"best":74,"last":74,"total":78,"attempts":2},"ex2":{"best":78,"last":78,"total":82,"attempts":2},"ex4":{"best":28,"last":28,"total":66,"attempts":1}}},"114046":{"activities":{"Formative Assessment":true},"logbook":{"quiz.unit-quiz-c7a71582-621f-4e02-a1ca-5132ecbdf537.picks":"{\"0\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[2],\"disp\":[0,1,3,2]},\"1\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[3,0,2,1]},\"2\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[0,2,3,1]},\"3\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[2,3,1,0]},\"4\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[3,2,1,0]},\"5\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[2],\"disp\":[2,0,1,3]},\"6\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[2,1,0,3]},\"7\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[3],\"disp\":[1,3,0,2]},\"8\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0],\"disp\":[3,1,0,2]},\"9\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[2,3,0,1]}}","exq.manual-activity-7fde574d-46c8-4c5e-aa8b-c6e93011e93c.0":"Different storage types and access rights can be managed to control how data is stored and used on the network.\nHardware devices such as printers, computers, and servers can be monitored and controlled across the network.\nNetwork services and devices, including routers and internet connections, can be managed to ensure efficient network operation.","exq.manual-activity-7fde574d-46c8-4c5e-aa8b-c6e93011e93c.0.ok":false,"exq.manual-activity-7fde574d-46c8-4c5e-aa8b-c6e93011e93c.0.tries":"2","selfassess-0":true,"selfassess-1":true,"selfassess-2":true,"selfassess-3":true,"selfassess.savedAt":"2026-09-25T11:50:40.127Z","exq.manual-activity-7fde574d-46c8-4c5e-aa8b-c6e93011e93c.1":"A user has limited access rights and can only use files, programs, and resources that permission has been granted for.\nAn operator has more access than a user and can perform routine tasks such as backups, monitoring, and system maintenance.\nAn administrator has the highest access level and can manage users, security settings, network resources, and system configurations.","exq.manual-activity-7fde574d-46c8-4c5e-aa8b-c6e93011e93c.1.ok":true,"exq.manual-activity-7fde574d-46c8-4c5e-aa8b-c6e93011e93c.1.tries":"2","exq.manual-activity-7fde574d-46c8-4c5e-aa8b-c6e93011e93c.2":"Access can be controlled by requiring a unique username, password, or biometric identification before users can log in.\nFolder permissions can restrict which users are allowed to view, create, modify, or delete files.\nFile access permissions determine who can read, edit, copy, or delete specific files.\nAccess can be limited to certain dates or times to improve security and control resource usage.\nAccess can be restricted to specific computers, networks, or physical locations for security purposes.","exq.manual-activity-7fde574d-46c8-4c5e-aa8b-c6e93011e93c.2.ok":true,"exq.manual-activity-7fde574d-46c8-4c5e-aa8b-c6e93011e93c.2.tries":"1","exq.manual-activity-7fde574d-46c8-4c5e-aa8b-c6e93011e93c.3":"An access audit trail records who accessed a system, file, or resource and when the access occurred.\nIt helps detect unauthorized access attempts and identifies users who violate security policies.\nIt provides a record of system activities that can be used for monitoring, investigations, and compliance purposes.","exq.manual-activity-7fde574d-46c8-4c5e-aa8b-c6e93011e93c.3.ok":true,"exq.manual-activity-7fde574d-46c8-4c5e-aa8b-c6e93011e93c.3.tries":"1","slidegate.0":true,"slidegate.1":true,"slidegate.2":true,"slidegate.3":true,"slidegate.4":true,"slidegate.6":true,"slidegate.7":true,"slidegate.8":true,"slidegate.9":true,"exq.manual-activity-5ddb79c1-37d7-4328-ae72-5dd4872fd04b.0":"The faster the computers, switches and routers process data, the quicker the LAN responds to user requests.\nA transmission line with higher bandwidth can carry more data per second, reducing network delays.\nWhen many data packets arrive at the same time, they must wait in queues, increasing response time.\nEach network device requires time to examine and process packets before forwarding them, which affects response time.\nLarger messages and additional protocol headers require more transmission and processing time on the network.\nPoor quality transmission causes errors and retransmissions, resulting in slower response times and reduced performance.","exq.manual-activity-5ddb79c1-37d7-4328-ae72-5dd4872fd04b.0.ok":true,"exq.manual-activity-5ddb79c1-37d7-4328-ae72-5dd4872fd04b.0.tries":"1","exq.manual-activity-5ddb79c1-37d7-4328-ae72-5dd4872fd04b.1":"Analysing data helps to identify errors, weaknesses and problem areas that may affect performance.\nData analysis enables informed decision-making by providing accurate information about existing problems.\nIdentifying problems early allows corrective action to be taken before the problems become more serious.","exq.manual-activity-5ddb79c1-37d7-4328-ae72-5dd4872fd04b.1.ok":true,"exq.manual-activity-5ddb79c1-37d7-4328-ae72-5dd4872fd04b.1.tries":"1","exq.manual-activity-5ddb79c1-37d7-4328-ae72-5dd4872fd04b.2":"Diagnostic tools collect data for diagnosis, helping technicians determine the cause of system and network problems.\nDiagnostic tools help identify faults, errors and the causes of problems more quickly.\nDiagnostic tools provide information that supports decision making when troubleshooting, repairing or upgrading systems.","exq.manual-activity-5ddb79c1-37d7-4328-ae72-5dd4872fd04b.2.ok":true,"exq.manual-activity-5ddb79c1-37d7-4328-ae72-5dd4872fd04b.2.tries":"2","exq.manual-activity-5ddb79c1-37d7-4328-ae72-5dd4872fd04b.3":"Faster processors execute instructions more quickly, reducing processing delays and improving overall system performance.\nUpgrading network interface cards increases data transfer speeds and improves network communication efficiency.\nImproved network protocols manage data transmission more efficiently, reducing errors and increasing performance.\nUsing a faster hard drive or SSD reduces data access times and speeds up system operations.\nHigher-quality transmission media supports faster data transfer rates and reduces signal interference\nIncreasing RAM allows more programs and data to be processed simultaneously, improving system performance.","exq.manual-activity-5ddb79c1-37d7-4328-ae72-5dd4872fd04b.3.ok":true,"exq.manual-activity-5ddb79c1-37d7-4328-ae72-5dd4872fd04b.3.tries":"1","exq.manual-activity-6026ddc0-7a48-4de9-9a7e-3619ba641c62.0":"Suppliers- Pros: specialist knowledge, warranty and support, Access to latest technology. Cons: Higher cost, less control, May not understand specific needs.\nThird party professionals- Pros: Wide range of expertise, flexible service options, good for specialized support. Cons: Ongoing service costs, response time may vary, less direct control.\nLocal expertise- Pros: Better understanding of organisational needs,greater control, fatser response times, can be more cost- effective in the long term. Cons: Requieres skilled staff, training and retention costs, may struggle with highly specialised issues.","exq.manual-activity-6026ddc0-7a48-4de9-9a7e-3619ba641c62.0.ok":false,"exq.manual-activity-6026ddc0-7a48-4de9-9a7e-3619ba641c62.0.tries":"2","exq.manual-activity-6026ddc0-7a48-4de9-9a7e-3619ba641c62.1":"","exq.manual-activity-6026ddc0-7a48-4de9-9a7e-3619ba641c62.1.ok":false,"exq.manual-activity-6026ddc0-7a48-4de9-9a7e-3619ba641c62.1.tries":"","practical.pdf.name":"","practical.pdf.surname":"","practical.pdf.full-names":"","practical.pdf.organisation":"","practical.pdf.unit-dept":"","practical.pdf.email":"","practical.pdf.telephone":"","learner-workbook.cover-name":"Anele","learner-workbook.cover-surname":"Khanyile","learner-workbook.cover-id":"0410271117088","learner-workbook.name":"Anele Khanyile","learner-workbook.organisation":"Investec","learner-workbook.unit-dept":"IT Desktop Support","learner-workbook.facilitator":"Andre Snell","learner-workbook.date-started":"2026-10-08","learner-workbook.full-names":"Anele Khanyile ","learner-workbook.learner-number":"0410271117088","learner-workbook.org-2":"Investec","learner-workbook.dept-2":"IT Desktop Support","learner-workbook.telephone":"0677521373","learner-workbook.email":"anele.khanyile@investec.com","learner-workbook.venue":"","learner-workbook.outcome-1.1.answer":"Computers or workstations are the devices used by users to access and share resources on the Local Area Network (LAN).\nNetwork Interface Cards (NICs) allow computers and other devices to connect and communicate with the LAN.\nSwitches connect multiple devices within the LAN and forward data to the correct destination.\nRouters connect the LAN to other networks, such as the Internet, and direct network traffic.\nEthernet cables provide the physical connection that enables data transfer between devices on the LAN.\nWireless Access Points (WAPs) allow wireless devices such as laptops and smartphones to connect to the LAN.","learner-workbook.task-mark.1":"{\"awarded\":5,\"maxMarks\":5,\"feedback\":\"Excellent identification of key physical components of a LAN, including devices, NICs, switches, routers, cables, and wireless access points. The answer is comprehensive and accurate.\",\"incorrectSegments\":[]}","learner-workbook.outcome-1.2.answer":"Network Access Control (NAC) is a network security system that controls and monitors access to a network by ensuring that only authorized users and compliant devices can connect to network resources. It helps protect the network by verifying user identities, checking device security requirements, and preventing unauthorized access.","learner-workbook.task-mark.2":"{\"awarded\":5,\"maxMarks\":5,\"feedback\":\"The learner provides a clear and accurate definition of Network Access Control (NAC), covering its purpose to control and monitor network access, ensuring only authorized users and compliant devices connect, and mentioning verification of user identities and device security. This matches the expected understanding fully.\",\"incorrectSegments\":[]}","learner-workbook.outcome-1.3.answer":"Audit trails are chronological records that track and document all activities, transactions, and changes made within a computer system or network. They help organizations monitor user actions, detect unauthorized access, investigate security incidents, ensure compliance with policies and regulations, and maintain accountability by providing evidence of who performed specific actions and when those actions occurred\nBenefits:\nTrack user and system activities.\nDetect security breaches and unauthorized access.\nSupport investigations and troubleshooting.\nEnsure compliance with laws, policies, and standards.","learner-workbook.task-mark.3":"{\"awarded\":5,\"maxMarks\":5,\"feedback\":\"The learner clearly defines audit trails as chronological records tracking activities and changes within systems, matching the model answer's meaning. They effectively outline key benefits and objectives, including monitoring user actions, detecting unauthorized access, supporting investigations, ensuring compliance, and maintaining accountability. The answer is comprehensive and well-expressed in the learner's own words.\",\"incorrectSegments\":[]}","learner-workbook.outcome-2.4.answer":"Local Area Network (LAN) performance issues are problems that reduce the speed, reliability, and efficiency of communication between devices on a network. Common LAN performance issues include network congestion, where too many devices compete for bandwidth and slow down data transmission; faulty network cables or hardware, which can cause data loss and connection failures; incorrect network configurations, which may lead to communication delays; network interference, particularly in wireless LANs, which weakens signal quality; and insufficient bandwidth, which results in slow network performance when handling large amounts of data.","learner-workbook.task-mark.4":"{\"awarded\":5,\"maxMarks\":5,\"feedback\":\"The learner provides a clear and comprehensive explanation of local area network performance issues, covering key factors such as network congestion, faulty hardware, incorrect configurations, interference, and insufficient bandwidth. This demonstrates a thorough understanding of the topic.\",\"incorrectSegments\":[]}","learner-workbook.outcome-3.5.answer":"Local Area Network (LAN) support issues are problems that affect the operation, maintenance, and troubleshooting of devices and services on a network. Common LAN support issues include network connectivity failures, where users cannot access the network; IP address conflicts, where two devices are assigned the same IP address; hardware failures, such as faulty switches, routers, or network cables; software and configuration errors, which prevent devices from communicating properly; and security issues, such as malware or unauthorized access, which can disrupt network services and compromise data.","learner-workbook.task-mark.5":"{\"awarded\":5,\"maxMarks\":5,\"feedback\":\"The learner clearly explains a range of local area network support issues, including connectivity failures, IP conflicts, hardware failures, software/configuration errors, and security problems, matching the expected criteria well.\",\"incorrectSegments\":[]}","learner-workbook.outcome-4.6.answer":"Trojan Horses\n\nA Trojan Horse is malicious software that is disguised as a legitimate program. Common symptoms include unexpected programs running on the system, unusual system changes, and backdoors that allow data theft. Trojan Horses spread through email attachments, downloaded software, infected websites, and social engineering attacks.\n\nSpoofing\n\nSpoofing is the impersonation of a trusted source, such as a user, device, or website. Common symptoms include fake login pages, suspicious emails, unauthorized access, and misdirected data. Spoofing spreads through phishing emails, fake websites, IP or MAC address spoofing, and DNS spoofing.\n\nWorms (1)\n\nA worm is self-replicating malware that spreads across networks without user action. Common symptoms include slow network performance, high network traffic, unusual system activity, and spreading to other devices. Worms spread through network shares, vulnerable services, email, and removable media.\n\nWorms (2)\n\nAdvanced worms exploit known vulnerabilities to spread rapidly. Common symptoms include system crashes, disabled security tools, rapid spread across a LAN, and high resource usage. These worms spread by exploiting software flaws, open ports, network propagation, and do not require user interaction.\n\nAC 2: Prevention, Detection, and Eradication of Viruses\nPrevention\n\nVirus prevention involves stopping viruses before they enter a network. This can be achieved by keeping operating systems and software up to date, using reputable antivirus and anti-malware software, enabling and configuring firewalls, applying strong access controls and user permissions, being cautious with email attachments and links, disabling unnecessary services, and educating users about phishing and safe internet use.\n\nDetection\n\nVirus detection involves identifying viruses quickly and accurately. This can be done by using real-time antivirus scanning, monitoring network traffic for suspicious activity, checking system logs and event reports, using intrusion detection systems (IDS), performing regular scans, looking for unusual behavior such as slow performance, and using updated virus definitions or signatures.\n\nEradication\n\nVirus eradication involves removing the threat and restoring normal operation. This includes isolating infected devices from the network, running full antivirus or anti-malware scans, removing or quarantining infected files, patching exploited vulnerabilities, restoring clean files from backups if necessary, verifying that the virus has been removed, and monitoring the network to ensure that re-infection does not occur.","learner-workbook.task-mark.6":"{\"awarded\":5,\"maxMarks\":5,\"feedback\":\"The learner provides a detailed and accurate explanation of typical viruses on local area networks, including Trojan Horses, Spoofing, and Worms, covering their nature, symptoms, and methods of spread. The answer is comprehensive and well-structured, demonstrating clear understanding relevant to the question.\",\"incorrectSegments\":[]}","learner-workbook.date-completed":"2026-10-09"},"quizzes":{"unit-quiz-c7a71582-621f-4e02-a1ca-5132ecbdf537":{"best":8,"total":10,"attempts":2,"history":[{"score":8,"total":10,"date":"2026-09-25T11:41:45.206Z"},{"score":4,"total":10,"date":"2026-09-25T11:40:14.894Z"}]}},"exercises":{"manual-activity-7fde574d-46c8-4c5e-aa8b-c6e93011e93c":{"best":26,"last":26,"total":28,"attempts":1},"manual-activity-5ddb79c1-37d7-4328-ae72-5dd4872fd04b":{"best":34,"last":34,"total":36,"attempts":1},"manual-activity-6026ddc0-7a48-4de9-9a7e-3619ba641c62":{"best":8,"last":8,"total":16,"attempts":2}}},"114050":{"activities":{"Formative Assessment":true},"logbook":{"exq.qs114050b.0":"A sole trader is owned by one person - there are no partners or co-owners.\nNo formal registration, administration or termination is needed and no statutes regulate sole owners.\nIf the business becomes insolvent, the owner personally becomes insolvent.\n ","exq.qs114050b.0.ok":true,"exq.qs114050b.1":"A partnership is a business association between people who intend making and sharing profits.\nIt has a minimum of two and a maximum of 20 partners and is not a legal person.\nPartners are jointly and severally liable for the partnership's debts.\n ","exq.qs114050b.1.ok":false,"exq.qs114050b.2":"Registered under the Companies Act as a legal person - This means the Limited Co is officially recognised by law as its own legal entity, separate from the people who own it.\nLimits the owners' liability - This means the owners usually do not lose all their personal possessions if the business cannot pay its debts.\nBetter able to acquire capital - This means the Limited Co can raise money more easily from investors or shareholders to grow the business.","exq.qs114050b.2.ok":true,"exq.qs114050b.6":"Companies that are profit-driven interest with clients by selling goods and services at a higher than the cost price to make a profit. Some businesses aim for profit maximisation while others are satisfied with enough profit to keep the owners comfortable.","exq.qs114050b.6.ok":true,"exq.qs114050b.7":"These companies have a charitable purpose and are led by beliefs, not profit. They interact with clients not to make money but to help the community and support a good cause based on their beliefs and values.","exq.qs114050b.7.ok":true,"exq.qs114050b.3":"A private company (Pty) Ltd is a business that is owned by one or more shareholders and is  registered as a separate legal entity from its owners. Its shares are not offered to the public and can only be transferred according to the company's rules. Its names ends with (Pty)Ltd and is subject to fewer legal requirements. A private company has between one and 50 members ( shareholders) and at least one director.","exq.qs114050b.3.ok":true,"exq.qs114050b.4":"Private Company (Pty) \nA private Company (Pty) Ltd is a business that is owned by one or more shareholders and is not allowed to sell its shares to the general public legal.","exq.qs114050b.4.ok":true,"exq.qs114050b.5":"A sole trader interacts directly with clients during buying and selling activities.\nThe owner is usually responsible for dealing with customers, processing sales, and purchasing goods and services needed for the business.","exq.qs114050b.5.ok":true,"exq.qs114050b.8":"A service to member rather than profit _ social clubs do not have clients/customers in the traditional business sense, they have members","exq.qs114050b.8.ok":true,"exq.qs114050b.9":"These businesses operate in a market and the size of the market determines how many clients they can serve and how big the business can grow. \nThese businesses need capital fund them, premises to work from, staffing to provide services, and they carry the risk of losing money.\nThese businesses operate in a competitive environment where there is competition from other businesses offering similar services to the same clients.","exq.qs114050b.9.ok":true,"quiz.q-business.picks":"{\"0\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"1\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"2\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"3\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"4\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"5\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"6\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"7\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"8\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"9\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]}}","exq.qs114050sys.0":"A system is a collection of parts that work together as a whole in an orderly arrangement according to a plan to achieve a specific goal or purpose. The whole is the complete system.The parts are the different components or subsystems that make up the system. These parts are organized and connected in a planned way so that they can work together effectively.If one part fails, it can affect the performance of the entire system","exq.qs114050sys.0.ok":true,"exq.qs114050sys.1":"nput Input is the data, materials, or resources that are entered into a system ProcessProcess is the activity that transforms the input into something useful. output-Copilot said:Output (Theoretical Component of a System) Output is the final result or information that a system produces after processing the input. It is what the system delivers to the user or another system to achieve its purpose. Key PointsOutput is the end product of the system's processing activities.It can be in the form of information, goods, services, or actions. The quality of the output depends on the quality of the input and processing.ExamplesIn a computer system, output may be information displayed on a monitor, printed on paper, or played through speakers.In a manufacturing system, output is the finished product.In a school system, output may be learners who have gained knowledge and skills.Example Using a CalculatorInput: Numbers entered by the user (e.g., 5 + 3)Process: The calculator performs the calculation.Output: The answer displayed on the screen","exq.qs114050sys.1.ok":true,"exq.qs114050sys.2":"Collects, stores, modifies and retrieves transactions: TPS records everyday business activities and keeps the information organised for future use. Transaction creates or changes data: Examples include making a purchase, depositing money into a bank account, or updating customer information.ACID test, rapid response and reliability: TPS ensures transactions are processed correctly, data remains accurate, and the system responds quickly even when handling many transactions.","exq.qs114050sys.2.ok":false,"exq.qs114050sys.4":"An MIS provides managers with information needed for planning, controlling, and decision-making. It serves decisions at the operational, tactical and strategic levels of the organisation.","exq.qs114050sys.4.ok":true,"exq.qs114050sys.3":"ts software includes word processing, spreadsheets, database management systems, CAD, project management and expert systems. In Information Systems (KWS Example) A Knowledge Work System (KWS) supports employees such as engineers, scientists, designers, and IT specialists by providing tools to create, analyse, and share knowledge. For example, a software developer uses programming tools and databases to create new applications A Knowledge Work System helps people deal with problems requiring technical expertise or kno\n \n5. An MIS provides managers with information needed for planning, controlling, and decision-making. It serves decisions at the operational, tactical and strategic levels of the organisation.","exq.qs114050sys.3.ok":true,"exq.qs114050apps.0":"Word processors can be used in business for creating , editing and storing business documents like letters, reports and invoices in the computer\nThey have an effect of improving business efficiency and producing professional looking documents\nTheir functions include formatting text, checking spelling and grammar, and doing mail merge to create many letters quickly","exq.qs114050apps.0.ok":true,"exq.qs114050apps.1":"Spreadsheets are used in business for budgeting, payroll, sales records and doing calculations and financial analysis quickly.\nTheir functions include using formulas, automatic calculations, creating charts and graphs, and doing what-if analysis for forecasting business performance.\n.The effect is that they save time, reduce calculation errors, improve decision making and present a professional financial image for the business.","exq.qs114050apps.1.ok":true,"quiz.q-systems.picks":"{\"0\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"1\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"2\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"3\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"4\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"5\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[3]},\"6\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"7\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"8\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"9\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1]}}","exq.qs114050apps.1.tries":"2","exq.qs114050apps.2":"Databases store and organise large amounts of business information, making it easy for employees to access and update records quickly.\nStructured records managed and queried by a DBMS .\nDatabases reduce data duplication and errors, improving accuracy, increasing efficiency, and saving the business time and money.","exq.qs114050apps.2.ok":false,"exq.qs114050apps.2.tries":"2","exq.qs114050apps.3":"Graphics are used in advertising and marketing to attract customers' attention and promote products or services. This helps businesses increase sales and build brand awareness.\nGraphics are used to create and edit visual content such as images, illustrations, posters, and promotional materials. This helps businesses communicate information clearly and attract customers.\nGraphics help businesses create a professional image at a low in-house cost by designing logos, advertisements, and marketing materials themselves instead of outsourcing the work.","exq.qs114050apps.3.ok":true,"exq.qs114050apps.3.tries":"2","exq.qs114050apps.4":"Integrated office suites allow users to move and share data between applications such as word processors, spreadsheets, and presentation software. This saves time and reduces duplicate work.\nCloud-based integrated office suites such as Microsoft 365 and Google Workspace allow employees to access and work on documents from different locations. This improves collaboration and business productivity.\nintegrated office suites offer one subscription, shared data, and transferable skills across applications. This reduces software costs, makes data easier to share, and helps employees work more effectively.","exq.qs114050apps.4.ok":true,"exq.qs114050apps.4.tries":"2","slidegate.18":true},"exercises":{"qs114050b":{"best":38,"last":38,"total":48,"attempts":1},"qs114050sys":{"best":18,"last":18,"total":24,"attempts":2},"qs114050apps":{"best":20,"last":20,"total":30,"attempts":1}},"quizzes":{"q-business":{"best":10,"total":10,"attempts":2,"history":[{"score":10,"total":10,"date":"2026-08-27T16:29:57.838Z"},{"score":6,"total":10,"date":"2026-08-27T16:27:25.242Z"}]},"q-systems":{"best":8,"total":10,"attempts":1,"history":[{"score":8,"total":10,"date":"2026-08-28T10:57:43.892Z"}]}}},"114051":{"activities":{"Formative Assessment":true},"logbook":{"quiz.q-meeting-types.picks":"{\"0\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"1\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"2\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"3\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"4\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"5\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]}}","quiz.q-decisions-conventions.picks":"{\"0\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"1\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"2\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"3\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"4\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"5\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]}}","exq.qs114051a.0":"Contract meetings â Contract meetings are held to discuss contracts with clients and suppliers.\nTechnical review meetings â Technical review meetings are held to evaluate technical work and related activities.\nProject review meetings â Project review meetings are held to track project progress throughout the project.\n ","exq.qs114051a.0.ok":true,"exq.qs114051a.1":".\nDemocratic meeting â All members of the group are encouraged to participate in discussions, and decisions are made by the group, often through voting or agreement. Autocratic meeting â The chairperson controls the meeting and makes the decisions, with little or no input from the other members.\n ","exq.qs114051a.1.ok":true,"exq.qs114051a.2":"In a facilitative meeting, the facilitator guides the process by helping the discussion stay structured and focused on the meeting objectives. In a facilitative meeting, the group participates and produces the outcome by discussing ideas and working together to reach decisions. A facilitative meeting is a group effort: a facilitator guides the process while staying neutral, and the group generates the ideas and reaches the outcome together.\n ","exq.qs114051a.2.ok":true,"exq.qs114051a.3":"Voting â Each member votes and the option with the majority is adopted. Consensus â Discussion continues until every member can accept the decision. Criteria-based rating â Options are scored against agreed criteria and the highest score wins. Ranking â Members place the options in order of preference and the rankings are combined. Paired comparisons â Options are compared two at a time and the overall preferred option is selected.","exq.qs114051a.3.ok":true,"exq.qs114051a.4":"A note taker should have a technical background because they understand the technical terminology used during discussions and can record information correctly. A note taker should have a technical background so that the minutes capture decisions accurately without misunderstanding important technical details. A note taker should have a technical background because they can follow the technical discussion and understand the points being made by participants.\n","exq.qs114051a.4.ok":true,"exq.qs114051b.0":"Before a technical practtitioners meeting, the venue must be booked and set up.the required facilities must be arranged and all technology must be setup and tested\nFacilities arranged: all required facilities such as seating, tables, lighting, air conditioning, and refreshments must be available and ready before the meeting.\ntechnology must be set up and tested beforehand, including computers, projectors, internet connections, microphones, and conferencing equipment.\nMeeting materials must be prepared and available, including agendas, reports, handouts, and any supporting documentation required by participants.","exq.qs114051b.0.ok":true,"quiz.q-prep-chair.picks":"{\"0\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"1\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"2\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"3\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"4\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"5\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]}}","quiz.q-followup.picks":"{\"0\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"1\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"2\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"3\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]},\"4\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0]}}","exq.qs114051b.1":"Intended outcomes of the meeting must be clear, concise and documented before the meeting as it keeps the meeting focused on its purpose, the agenda is built around the outcomes,Sucess can be measured against the outcomes\nClear, concise, documented outcomes keep the meeting focused on its purpose â participants know what must be achieved.\nThe agenda can be planned and structured around the documented outcomes.\nAfter the meeting, success can be measured and evaluated against the documented outcomes.\nThe agenda can be planned and structured around the documented outcomes.","exq.qs114051b.1.ok":true,"exq.qs114051b.2":"Participants must be invited timeously so that they have enough time to prepare relevant information and reports needed for the technical practicitioners meeting . Inviting timeously ensures that participants can arrange their schedules and confti\nParticipants must be invited timeously so that they can arrange their schedules, avoid clashes with other commitments, and ensure they are available to attend the meeting.\nInviting participants early allows them to review the agenda and supporting documents beforehand, enabling more effective participation and better decision-making during the meeting.","exq.qs114051b.2.ok":true,"selfassess-0":true,"selfassess-1":true,"selfassess-2":true,"selfassess-3":true,"selfassess-4":true,"selfassess-5":true,"selfassess-6":true,"selfassess.savedAt":"2026-09-04T12:04:22.298Z","exq.qs114051c.0":"When members help create the rules, they feel included and are more likely to follow and respect the agreed guidelines throughout the meeting.\nthe chairperson works through the agenda item by item. The chairperson keeps discussions focused on the current topic and prevents members from moving onto unrelated issues. The chairperson watches the time allocated to each agenda item.\nInvite quiet members by name to give input and use round-robin turns so everyone speaks. Keep the debate focused on issues, not people. The chairperson should encourage members to discuss the problem or topic objectively and avoid personal criticism. This helps reduce conflict and maintains a respectful atmosphere. Summarise areas of agreement before moving on. By highlighting points that members already agree on, the chairperson reduces misunderstandings, keeps the meeting focused, and makes it easier to resolve remaining differences.","exq.qs114051c.0.ok":false,"exq.qs114051b.3":"Participants must be invited timeously so that they can confirm their attendance, allowing the organiser to know who will be present at the meeting.\nearly invitations give participants enough time to prepare the necessary information, reports, and documentation required for discussion during the meeting.\nThe meeting invitation and relevant meeting details must be distributed early so participants can prepare properly and attend the meeting.","exq.qs114051b.3.ok":false,"exq.qs114051b.0.tries":"2","exq.qs114051b.1.tries":"1","exq.qs114051b.2.tries":"2","exq.qs114051b.3.tries":"2","exq.qs114051c.0.tries":"2","exq.qs114051c.1":"The chairperson follows the order of topics listed on the agenda and discusses each item one at a time.\nThe chairperson keeps discussions focused on the current agenda item and redirects members when they go off topic.\nThe chairperson manages the meeting time effectively so that all agenda items are covered before the meeting ends.","exq.qs114051c.1.ok":true,"exq.qs114051c.1.tries":"1","exq.qs114051c.2":"the chairperson should encourage every member to contribute by giving everyone an equal chance to speak and share their opinions respectfully.\nThe chairperson should use active listening and remain neutral, ensuring disagreements are managed calmly and discussions stay focused on the topic.\nThe chairperson should enforce agreed meeting rules, preventing interruptions and ensuring members treat each other with respect.","exq.qs114051c.2.ok":false,"exq.qs114051c.3":"Important and urgent topics should be discussed first so that critical decisions are made before time runs out.\nEach topic gets a time allocation in proportion to its importance.\nLess critical items are moved to the end of the agenda, deferred or carried over to the next meeting.","exq.qs114051c.3.ok":true,"exq.qs114051c.2.tries":"2","exq.qs114051c.3.tries":"2","exq.qs114051c.4":"The chairperson must ensure that every decision is agreed upon by the members and reflects the outcome of the discussion.\nThe chairperson must ensure that every decision is clearly recorded in the meeting minutes for future reference and accountability.\nThe chairperson must ensure that decisions are lawful, fair, and aligned with the organisation's rules and objectives.","exq.qs114051c.4.ok":false,"exq.qs114051c.4.tries":"2","exq.qs114051d.0":"The minutes of a technical practitioners meeting are accurate and acceptable when they record attendance and apologies correctly.\nThis shows who was present, who was absent, and whether the meeting had the required participants. Minutes must capture each discussion, decision and action with its owner and timeframe.\nMinutes must follow the organization's minute format and template as required by organizational policy.\nThe minutes should be checked for accuracy, approved if required, and distributed to all participants on time. This ensures that everyone receives the correct information and can act on the decisions made.","exq.qs114051d.0.ok":true,"exq.qs114051d.0.tries":"1","exq.qs114051d.1":"Decisions are communicated in the format the organisation requires â minutes, e-mail summaries or reports\nTo all affected stakeholders.\nWithin the required timeframe.","exq.qs114051d.1.ok":true,"exq.qs114051d.1.tries":"2","exq.qs114051d.2":"The summary lists each topic discussed and its outcome or decision.\nThe summary lists the actions arising, each with the responsible person and a deadline.\nThe summary should identify any items that were not completed or fully discussed and that need to be carried over to the next meeting for further consideration.\nn. The summary is presented in the format the organization requires.","exq.qs114051d.2.ok":true,"exq.qs114051d.2.tries":"1"},"quizzes":{"q-meeting-types":{"best":6,"total":6,"attempts":1,"history":[{"score":6,"total":6,"date":"2026-09-04T08:36:41.219Z"}]},"q-decisions-conventions":{"best":6,"total":6,"attempts":2,"history":[{"score":6,"total":6,"date":"2026-09-04T08:39:49.457Z"},{"score":2,"total":6,"date":"2026-09-04T08:38:24.076Z"}]},"q-prep-chair":{"best":6,"total":6,"attempts":1,"history":[{"score":6,"total":6,"date":"2026-09-04T11:08:18.469Z"}]},"q-followup":{"best":5,"total":5,"attempts":2,"history":[{"score":5,"total":5,"date":"2026-09-04T11:11:48.014Z"},{"score":3,"total":5,"date":"2026-09-04T11:09:48.243Z"}]}},"exercises":{"qs114051a":{"best":26,"last":26,"total":32,"attempts":1},"qs114051b":{"best":20,"last":20,"total":26,"attempts":1},"qs114051c":{"best":10,"last":10,"total":30,"attempts":3},"qs114051d":{"best":18,"last":18,"total":22,"attempts":1}}},"114055":{"activities":{"Summative Assessment":true,"Formative Assessment":true,"Lesson & Training Aids":true},"logbook":{"exq.ex1.0":"Competence and keeping up to date\nSecurity and privacy\nAccountability and responsibility \n","exq.ex1.0.ok":true,"exq.ex1.2":"The Black Infromation Technology \nInfluencing policy and representing members\n","exq.ex1.2.ok":true,"exq.ex1.1":"The Computer Society of South Africa \nElevating ICT capability and professionalism\nPublishes the codes of practice and conduct\nRepresents practitioners and lobbies government","exq.ex1.1.ok":true,"exq.ex1.3":"Helps SA's IT market trade internationally -founded  2006 empowers the market\nThe world's largest\nA trade union federation- Founded in 2006","exq.ex1.3.ok":true,"exq.ex1.4":"Represents and promotes employers' interests \nPromotes consistent standards of professionalism\nOfficial trade and employee body of the ICTe industry- Founded in 1934 and it was renamed after ITA","exq.ex1.4.ok":true,"exq.ex1.5":"Competence, management and contracting\nSecurity , development, Implementation and live systems\nSet out by the CSSA Code of Practice","exq.ex1.5.ok":true,"exq.ex2.0":"Training on an equal opportunity basis \nProviding training for disadvantaged people\nInitiate community development programs","exq.ex2.0.ok":true,"exq.ex2.1":"Piracy is essentially theft because it involves taking software without paying for it\nDamage to the software industry and results in job losses because companies lose revenue.\nBSA campaigns create awareness as well as legal settlements and court presecution","exq.ex2.1.ok":true,"exq.ex2.2":"copyright legislation and TRIPS compliance\nBSA prosecution and out-of-court settlements\nSAFACT and SAPS enforcement action\nonline marketplaces policing their platforms;","exq.ex2.2.ok":true,"project.upload":"{\"name\":\"Ethics 114055.docx\",\"type\":\"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document\",\"size\":13797,\"uploadedAt\":\"2026-09-03T19:07:46.926Z\",\"path\":\"6ac4a7ae-93ff-46cf-bba0-e3eb925c2c59/logbook/mtlwdje6-Ethics_114055.docx\"}"},"exercises":{"ex1":{"best":40,"last":40,"total":48,"attempts":1},"ex2":{"best":22,"last":22,"total":24,"attempts":1}},"quiz":{"best":15,"total":15,"attempts":1,"history":[{"score":15,"total":15,"date":"2026-08-15T14:15:25.260Z"}]}},"114059":{"activities":{"Lesson & Training Aids":true,"Formative Assessment":true},"logbook":{"exq.manual-activity-61e25cd8-8548-4af8-a898-1bd559abddb6.0":"Purpose of cost/benefit analysis â Cost/benefit analysis helps decide whether a proposed change or project is worth implementing by comparing its total expected costs against its total expected benefits.\nComponents of cost/benefit analysis â The analysis includes identifying all costs (one-off and ongoing) and benefits (often received over time), then calculating metrics like payback period to assess when benefits repay costs.\nSubjectivity in estimating benefits â Estimating benefits can involve subjective judgments, especially when including intangible factors like risks or reputation, which must be assigned monetary values.\nFormal and informal uses â Cost/benefit analysis can be a formal project appraisal tool or an informal decision- making approach, both involving weighing  costs against benefits to choose the best option.\nGraphical break-even analysis â Break-even point can be found graphically by plotting costs and income against output quantity, where the lines cross indicates when benefits equal costs.","exq.manual-activity-61e25cd8-8548-4af8-a898-1bd559abddb6.0.ok":true,"exq.manual-activity-61e25cd8-8548-4af8-a898-1bd559abddb6.0.tries":"1","exq.manual-activity-5bf394d9-7a1c-4084-b567-7058607a1d22.0":"The project is divided into smaller logical components so that each task can be estimated more accurately.\nThe first stage in estimating time accurately is to fully understand what you need to achieve. This involves reviewing the task in detail so that there are no unknowns.. The best way to review the job is to list all tasks in full detail. Once you have a detailed list of all the tasks that you must achieve, make your best guess at how long each task will take to complete\nensure that within your estimate you also allow time for project management, detailed project planning, liaison with outside bodies, meetings, quality assurance and any supporting documentation necessary.","exq.manual-activity-5bf394d9-7a1c-4084-b567-7058607a1d22.0.ok":true,"exq.manual-activity-5bf394d9-7a1c-4084-b567-7058607a1d22.0.tries":"2","exq.manual-activity-5bf394d9-7a1c-4084-b567-7058607a1d22.1":"Time must be allocated for implementing interfaces that allow different system components to communicate correctly.\nThe estimate should include testing the interfaces to ensure data is transferred accurately between components.\nAdditional time should be included for fixing interface problems and verifying that all components work together successfully.","exq.manual-activity-5bf394d9-7a1c-4084-b567-7058607a1d22.1.ok":true,"exq.manual-activity-5bf394d9-7a1c-4084-b567-7058607a1d22.1.tries":"1","selfassess-0":true,"selfassess-1":true,"selfassess-2":true,"selfassess-3":true,"selfassess.savedAt":"2026-09-18T11:27:17.745Z"},"exercises":{"manual-activity-61e25cd8-8548-4af8-a898-1bd559abddb6":{"best":8,"last":8,"total":10,"attempts":2},"manual-activity-5bf394d9-7a1c-4084-b567-7058607a1d22":{"best":12,"last":12,"total":12,"attempts":1}}},"114074":{"logbook":{"exq.manual-activity-31633fbd-2077-4d62-bc75-9fbc9fc60c0f.0":"A Local Area Network (LAN) connects devices within a limited area, while a Wide Area Network (WAN) connects networks across large geographical areas.\nA star topology connects all devices to a central switch or hub, while a bus topology connects devices along a single communication cable.\nIP addressing provides a unique logical address to each device on a network so that data can be routed to the correct destination.\nMAC addressing identifies each network device by using a unique physical hardware address assigned to its network interface.\nThe IEEE and ISO are organizations that define network standards, and standards such as Ethernet and WiâFi provide industry network architectures for communication.","exq.manual-activity-8c8ceb6a-b9c1-4055-816d-28a8c9ed1959.0":"Baseband transmission uses the entire communication channel to send one signal at a time and is commonly used in Ethernet LANs.\nBroadband transmission divides the channel into multiple frequency bands, allowing several signals to be transmitted simultaneously.\nA token passing access protocol allows only the device holding the token to transmit data, preventing data collisions on the network.\nA network interface card (NIC) is a LAN component that enables a computer to connect and communicate with other devices on a network.\nAn incorrect IP address, subnet mask, or cable installation can cause communication failures and connectivity problems on a LAN.","exq.manual-activity-98aacadb-9f05-477a-8e3d-a73bcc9eb317.0":"WAN management issues include network security, bandwidth limitations, fault monitoring, and maintaining reliable communication between remote sites.\nA peer-to-peer LAN architecture allows computers to share resources directly with each other without a dedicated server.\nCircuit switching is a switching technique that establishes a dedicated communication path between two devices before data transmission begins.\nPacket switching is a switching technique that breaks data into packets, which are transmitted separately and reassembled at the destination.\nWAN management issues include network security, fault management, bandwidth control, and monitoring communication links between remote locations.","exq.manual-activity-31633fbd-2077-4d62-bc75-9fbc9fc60c0f.0.ok":false,"exq.manual-activity-8c8ceb6a-b9c1-4055-816d-28a8c9ed1959.0.ok":false,"exq.manual-activity-98aacadb-9f05-477a-8e3d-a73bcc9eb317.0.ok":false,"exq.manual-activity-31633fbd-2077-4d62-bc75-9fbc9fc60c0f.0.marks":"","exq.manual-activity-31633fbd-2077-4d62-bc75-9fbc9fc60c0f.0.tries":"1","exq.manual-activity-8c8ceb6a-b9c1-4055-816d-28a8c9ed1959.0.marks":"","exq.manual-activity-8c8ceb6a-b9c1-4055-816d-28a8c9ed1959.0.tries":"1","exq.manual-activity-98aacadb-9f05-477a-8e3d-a73bcc9eb317.0.marks":"","exq.manual-activity-98aacadb-9f05-477a-8e3d-a73bcc9eb317.0.tries":"1","exq.manual-activity-31633fbd-2077-4d62-bc75-9fbc9fc60c0f.0.reviewedText":"","exq.manual-activity-8c8ceb6a-b9c1-4055-816d-28a8c9ed1959.0.reviewedText":"","exq.manual-activity-98aacadb-9f05-477a-8e3d-a73bcc9eb317.0.reviewedText":"","videoengagement.viewCount.https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/QMpWkkqX1eM":"7"},"exercises":{"manual-activity-31633fbd-2077-4d62-bc75-9fbc9fc60c0f":{"best":4,"last":4,"total":10,"attempts":1},"manual-activity-8c8ceb6a-b9c1-4055-816d-28a8c9ed1959":{"best":4,"last":4,"total":10,"attempts":1},"manual-activity-98aacadb-9f05-477a-8e3d-a73bcc9eb317":{"best":2,"last":2,"total":10,"attempts":1}},"activities":{"Formative Assessment":true,"Lesson & Training Aids":true}},"HWSW":{"activities":{"Lesson & Training Aids":false,"Formative Assessment":true},"logbook":{"quiz.hwsw-day1.picks":"{\"0\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[0,2,1,3]},\"1\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[2,0,1,3]},\"2\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[3,1,0,2]},\"3\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1,0],\"disp\":[1,3,0,2]},\"4\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[0],\"disp\":[2,3,0,1]},\"5\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[3,0,2,1]},\"6\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[3,1,2,0]},\"7\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1,0],\"disp\":[1,3,2,0]},\"8\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[0,1,2,3]},\"9\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[2],\"disp\":[2,0,1,3]},\"10\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[3,0,1,2]},\"11\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[0,3,1,2]}}","quiz.hwsw-day2.picks":"{\"0\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[1,3,0,2]},\"1\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[0,1,3,2]},\"2\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[3,0,1],\"disp\":[3,0,2,1]},\"3\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[1,3,2,0]},\"4\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[3,1,2,0]},\"5\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[2,0,1,3]},\"6\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[0,2,1,3]},\"7\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[3,0,1,2]},\"8\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[3,1,0,2]},\"9\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[2],\"disp\":[3,2,0,1]},\"10\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[2,0,1],\"disp\":[2,3,0,1]},\"11\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[1,2,3,0]}}","quiz.hwsw-psu.picks":"{\"0\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[2],\"disp\":[1,3,0,2]},\"1\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[3,1,0,2]},\"2\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[3,0,2,1]},\"3\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[0,3,2,1]},\"4\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[2],\"disp\":[1,3,2,0]},\"5\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[2,1,0],\"disp\":[3,2,1,0]},\"6\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[2],\"disp\":[2,0,1,3]},\"7\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],\"disp\":[0,2,1,3]},\"8\":{\"kind\":\"order\",\"order\":[0,1,4,2,3,5,6,7]},\"9\":{\"kind\":\"match\",\"picks\":{\"0\":0,\"1\":1,\"2\":2,\"3\":3,\"4\":4}}}","exq.hwsw-identify.0":"Upgrade the computer's RAM because multiple browser tabs and Excel use a large amount of memory at the same time.\nMore RAM allows applications to stay in memory instead of continuously swapping data between RAM and the disk.\nReducing disk swapping decreases constant disk activity and significantly improves overall system performance and responsiveness.","exq.hwsw-identify.0.ok":true,"exq.hwsw-identify.0.tries":"2","exq.hwsw-identify.1":"An HDD stores data on spinning magnetic disks, while an SSD uses flash memory chips with no moving parts.\nSSDs provide much faster boot times, file access speeds, and application loading than traditional HDDs.\nBecause SSDs have no moving parts, they are more durable and less likely to fail from physical shock.\nHDDs usually offer more storage capacity for a lower cost, making them suitable for large data storage.\nFor a new laptop, I would specify an SSD because it delivers faster performance, better reliability, and improved battery efficiency.","exq.hwsw-identify.1.ok":true,"exq.hwsw-identify.1.tries":"2","exq.hwsw-identify.2":"The designer should use DisplayPort or HDMI because these ports support 4K resolution at high refresh rates.\nDisplayPort is often preferred for professional graphics work because it provides high bandwidth and excellent image quality.\nVGA should not be used because it is an older analog standard that cannot reliably support modern 4K high-refresh-rate displays.","exq.hwsw-identify.2.ok":true,"exq.hwsw-identify.2.tries":"1","exq.hwsw-identify.3":"I would recommend a laser printer because it is designed for high-volume printing in busy office environments.\nLaser printers print quickly and produce sharp, professional-looking text that is ideal for financial reports.\nThe cost per page is usually lower than inkjet printers, making laser printers more economical for 5,000 pages each month.","exq.hwsw-identify.3.ok":true,"exq.hwsw-identify.3.tries":"1","exq.hwsw-identify.4":"A network switch connects all the office Pc together so they can communicate and share resources on the local network.\nThe switch receives data from one device and sends it to the correct destination device on the network.\nA router connects the office network to the internet and manages traffic between the local network and external networks.\nThe router directs data packets to and from the internet, allowing office users to access online services and websites.","exq.hwsw-identify.4.ok":true,"exq.hwsw-identify.4.tries":"2"},"quizzes":{"hwsw-day1":{"best":12,"total":12,"attempts":3,"history":[{"score":12,"total":12,"date":"2026-09-11T08:27:11.788Z"},{"score":9,"total":12,"date":"2026-09-11T08:25:49.753Z"},{"score":9,"total":12,"date":"2026-09-09T17:56:44.033Z"}]},"hwsw-day2":{"best":11,"total":12,"attempts":1,"history":[{"score":11,"total":12,"date":"2026-09-09T18:02:26.116Z"}]},"hwsw-psu":{"best":9,"total":10,"attempts":3,"history":[{"score":9,"total":10,"date":"2026-09-11T09:27:35.049Z"},{"score":7,"total":10,"date":"2026-09-11T09:22:40.438Z"},{"score":7,"total":10,"date":"2026-09-09T18:09:56.435Z"}]}},"exercises":{"hwsw-identify":{"best":12,"last":12,"total":36,"attempts":3}}},"HWSW2":{"activities":{"Formative Assessment":true},"logbook":{"quiz.hwsw2-hardware.picks":"{\"0\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"picks\":[1],